OLAP Demo (ROLAP, MOLAP, HOLAP)

This project shows how businesses can analyze data using OLAP (Online Analytical Processing).
It uses a small company example with employees and departments to demonstrate three types of OLAP and common operations.

🔹 What’s Inside

ROLAP (Relational OLAP) – uses database queries to get insights, e.g. average salary by department.

MOLAP (Multidimensional OLAP) – creates a cube (like an Excel pivot table) to compare data, e.g. salary by age group and department.

HOLAP (Hybrid OLAP) – mixes both methods for flexible analysis.

We also demonstrate common OLAP operations:

Slice – look at one department.

Dice – filter data with multiple conditions.

Drill-down – go into details, e.g. salary per employee.

Roll-up – summarize, e.g. total salary per department.

Charts and heatmaps are used to make the results easy to understand.

📊 Example Data

Employees: Names, ages, salaries, department IDs.

Departments: Department IDs and names (HR, Engineering, Sales).

